{
  "uid": "bgp-optimizer",
  "title": "BGP Optimizer: live demo",
  "description": "Two providers, one optimizer: who carries the traffic and why.",
  "tags": [
    "bgp",
    "lab"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "red",
        "name": "Route changes (live)",
        "expr": "sum by (action) (increase(optimizer_route_changes_total{mode=\"live\"}[10s])) > 0.5",
        "step": "2s",
        "titleFormat": "route {{action}}",
        "textFormat": "optimizer (live)",
        "tagKeys": "action",
        "useValueForTime": false,
        "target": {
          "expr": "sum by (action) (increase(optimizer_route_changes_total{mode=\"live\"}[10s])) > 0.5",
          "refId": "Anno",
          "interval": "2s"
        }
      },
      {
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "yellow",
        "name": "Would-be changes (dry-run)",
        "expr": "sum by (action) (increase(optimizer_route_changes_total{mode=\"dry-run\"}[10s])) > 0.5",
        "step": "2s",
        "titleFormat": "route {{action}}",
        "textFormat": "optimizer (dry-run)",
        "tagKeys": "action",
        "useValueForTime": false,
        "target": {
          "expr": "sum by (action) (increase(optimizer_route_changes_total{mode=\"dry-run\"}[10s])) > 0.5",
          "refId": "Anno",
          "interval": "2s"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### What you are looking at\n\nOur network has **two internet providers**, **ISP-A** and **ISP-B**, and both can reach the same server.\nNormally all traffic to the server goes through **ISP-A**: that is the router's default (BGP) policy.\n\nThe **optimizer** keeps sending small test packets through *both* providers and measures how slow they are (**RTT**)\nand how many get lost (**loss**). When ISP-A becomes clearly worse for several checks in a row, it tells the router\nover BGP: *\"send this traffic through ISP-B\"*. When ISP-A is healthy again, it switches back **once**, after a minimum\nhold time, so traffic does not jump back and forth. If the optimizer itself crashes, the router immediately forgets\nits advice and falls back to ISP-A.\n\n**Red markers** on the graphs show the moments the optimizer moved the traffic.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Client traffic goes via",
      "description": "Measured on the client with traceroute: the ISP router its packets really pass through.",
